      "claim": "The attacks caused extensive destruction not justified by military necessity, violating article 8(b)(iv) of the Rome Statute.",
      "reasoning": "The artillery bombardment produced large‑scale damage to civilian infrastructure and forced the displacement of a substantial civilian population, while the Trial Chamber found no concrete and direct military advantage that could justify such damage. Article 8(b)(iv) criminalises \"Extensive destruction and appropriation of property, not justified by military necessity and carried out unlawfully and wantonly.\" The factual record therefore meets the elements of this provision, rendering the attacks unlawful.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
